#: ../../technical/articles/048-interactive-flows-and-profile-bound-inventory-operations.md:10
msgid "Scope"
msgstr "Àmbit"

#: ../../technical/articles/048-interactive-flows-and-profile-bound-inventory-operations.md:12
msgid ""
"This chunk covers thirteen flow-substrate modules and five inventory "
"application modules (5,120 lines; 42,846 measured proxy tokens). I read "
"every assigned range in eight bounded pages. The flow code defines a "
"reusable declarative question engine, line frontend, "
"resume/review/checkpoint paths, and a wizard projection. The inventory "
"code exposes bucket-scoped ledger operations and profile-bound registered"
" workers. This is static inspection only: no interactive session, "
"checkpoint store, repository, terminal, or operation supervisor was run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/048-interactive-flows-and-profile-bound-inventory-operations.md:14
msgid "Interactive flow capabilities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/048-interactive-flows-and-profile-bound-inventory-operations.md:16
msgid ""
"A domain can describe a paged flow with typed widgets, requiredness, "
"closed choices, localized copy references, legal-reference zones, answer-"
"validator IDs, prior-answer visibility gates, section-exit validators, "
"and repeating groups. Definitions reject duplicate page IDs, gates that "
"do not point to earlier pages, repeating counts that lack an earlier "
"integer source, malformed widget/choice combinations, and incomplete per-"
"mode checkpoint declarations. Repeating groups are bounded (default "
"maximum 50). The wizard bridge projects the existing catalogue one way "
"into this substrate, preserving question IDs and gates and converting "
"choice-bearing text questions into select widgets; checkpoint policy "
"remains an explicit caller choice. Definition contracts "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/flows/definition.py`) Definition invariants "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/flows/definition.py`) Wizard projection "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/flows/wizard_projection.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/048-interactive-flows-and-profile-bound-inventory-operations.md:18
msgid ""
"The pure engine is the flow authority. It recomputes visible pages from "
"canonical answer tokens, commits only currently visible targets, runs "
"widget and registered validators, advances across section boundaries only"
" when exit checks pass, and produces immutable successor states. If an "
"answer controlling later visibility changes, already-entered dependents "
"become stale rather than being silently erased; shrinking a repeating "
"group similarly preserves its orphaned answers as stale. Compare-select "
"deferral remains visible and blocks submission until resolved. Review "
"includes visible rows and stale hidden orphans, aggregates "
"required/invalid/stale/deferred and cross-field blockers, and allows "
"submission only when none remain. State and transitions "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/flows/engine.py`) Answer and navigation "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/flows/engine.py`) Review gate "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/flows/review.py`) Submit eligibility "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/flows/review.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/048-interactive-flows-and-profile-bound-inventory-operations.md:20
msgid ""
"Built-in validators canonicalize booleans, choice sets, checkbox tokens, "
"integers, ISO dates, decimals, and paths before domain-specific "
"validators run. Decimal parsing rejects exponent notation and non-finite "
"values; validation verdicts pass interpolation context through the shared"
" redaction function. The line frontend is a sequential terminal surface "
"over the engine, supports injected I/O for headless driving, refuses "
"unsupported non-TTY/Windows console hosts before prompting, and provides "
"a grouped review/edit/restart/submit loop. Secret widgets use password "
"prompts and mask the previously committed answer in terminal output. One "
"data-handling caveat is explicit: the optional post-commit callback "
"receives the canonical answer, including a secret page’s raw value; the "
"code warns consumers not to log it but cannot enforce that rule. Widget "
"validation (`src/cadrumo/application/flows/validators.py`) Verdict "
"redaction (`src/cadrumo/application/flows/validators.py`) Line frontend "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/flows/line_frontend.py`) Secret callback "
"contract (`src/cadrumo/application/flows/line_frontend.py`) Terminal "
"masking (`src/cadrumo/application/flows/line_frontend.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/048-interactive-flows-and-profile-bound-inventory-operations.md:22
msgid ""
"The scripted driver consumes canonical tokens in the engine’s visible "
"order, allows defaults only for optional pages, refuses "
"underflow/overflow, and returns only a passing review. Resume treats "
"persisted answers as facts to revalidate against the current definition: "
"valid answers are recommitted in order, while invalid or now-unknown "
"answers remain stale and reviewable. It stores no derived cursor or "
"definition fingerprint. Scripted driver "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/flows/scripted.py`) Resume projection "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/flows/resume.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/048-interactive-flows-and-profile-bound-inventory-operations.md:24
msgid ""
"Checkpointing is a per-mode port. A mode declaring it unavailable refuses"
" a save; an available mode without an injected store refuses before the "
"frontend begins. The port contract requires domain-owned encrypted "
"persistence and forbids plaintext, but this package delegates that "
"requirement to implementations rather than verifying a concrete store. "
"Successful submit in the line frontend discards any checkpoint so a "
"submitted run does not remain resumable. Copy references resolve to "
"bundled locale text or registered domain resolvers; unresolved keys and "
"missing resolvers raise typed errors instead of leaking raw keys or "
"displaying blanks. Multiple resolvers for a kind are tried in "
"registration order, first non-`None` winning. Checkpoint contract and "
"save (`src/cadrumo/application/flows/checkpoint.py`) Copy resolution "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/flows/copy.py`) Page copy assembly "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/flows/copy.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/048-interactive-flows-and-profile-bound-inventory-operations.md:26
msgid "Inventory service and registered operations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/048-interactive-flows-and-profile-bound-inventory-operations.md:28
msgid ""
"The inventory application service coordinates a bucket-scoped repository "
"and bucket-event history port. It can create, list, show, append "
"movements, preview FIFO/PMP valuation through the domain calculator, "
"record a closing-authority bundle, and remove an activity/year ledger. "
"Purchase movements require the structured acquisition-cost authority and "
"reject legacy parallel cost fields. Movement candidates are validated "
"against the latest revision-guarded ledger before persistence, protecting"
" valuation checks from stale concurrent reads. Create/remove are likewise"
" delegated to guarded repository verbs because they rewrite a shared "
"ledger document. Closing-authority writes validate under the repository "
"guard, are replay-aware, and intentionally emit no bucket event because "
"the ledger and event repositories do not share a transaction. Service and"
" command contracts (`src/cadrumo/application/inventory/service.py`) "
"Service operations (`src/cadrumo/application/inventory/service.py`) "
"Movement guard and event (`src/cadrumo/application/inventory/service.py`)"
" Closing-authority transaction boundary "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/inventory/service.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/048-interactive-flows-and-profile-bound-inventory-operations.md:30
msgid ""
"The registered worker surface defines list, create, movement-add, "
"valuation-preview, and closing-authority operations. Requests are strict "
"hidden-input models with a profile ID; financial inputs cross the public "
"boundary as decimal strings. The executor requires the request payload "
"type and definition ID to match, binds work to the exact profile, "
"resolves read authority and adds commit permission for the mutating "
"operation IDs. It moves blocking repository work to a thread. Mutations "
"enter an irreversible cancellation section, mark effect `UNKNOWN` before "
"the work, await completion through cancellation, and then persist a typed"
" result or a known pre-commit refusal. This allows the operation "
"framework to reconcile ambiguous completion rather than reporting a false"
" no-effect result. Valuation preview is included among guarded operations"
" because it writes an audit event even though it does not change the "
"ledger. Request and worker contracts "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/inventory/registered_operation.py`) Executor "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/inventory/registered_operation.py`) "
"Mutation/cancellation handling "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/inventory/registered_operation.py`) Access "
"resolution (`src/cadrumo/application/inventory/registered_operation.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/048-interactive-flows-and-profile-bound-inventory-operations.md:32
msgid ""
"Private results are closed by operation/outcome and checked against the "
"terminal receipt before public projection. Ledger outputs keep "
"quantities, costs, and valuation results needed by the operator, but omit"
" acquisition-evidence contents and replace closing-authority documents "
"with fingerprints. Refusal projections carry bounded codes/reasons and "
"selected identifiers, not full exception text. Safe ledger projection "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/inventory/registered_operation.py`) "
"Receipt/result reconciliation "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/inventory/registered_operation.py`) Public "
"movement projection "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/inventory/registered_operation.py`) Port "
"boundary (`src/cadrumo/application/inventory/ports.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/048-interactive-flows-and-profile-bound-inventory-operations.md:34
msgid "Assessment and follow-up"
msgstr "Avaluació i seguiment"

#: ../../technical/articles/048-interactive-flows-and-profile-bound-inventory-operations.md:36
msgid ""
"The strongest flow properties are centralized transition semantics, "
"revalidation on resume, explicit stale/deferred blockers, and a shared "
"review gate across interactive and scripted entry. The main flow security"
" dependency is the caller-supplied checkpoint store’s compliance with "
"encrypted domain persistence; the secret commit callback is another "
"trusted boundary, and path-widget tokens are only lexically "
"accepted/expanded here, so filesystem consumers need their own path "
"authority. Flow state and definitions use frozen models around some "
"mutable dictionaries, with immutability also documented as a caller "
"convention."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/048-interactive-flows-and-profile-bound-inventory-operations.md:38
msgid ""
"Inventory has stronger admission and result boundaries: exact profile "
"correlation, scoped commit authority, typed hidden inputs, guarded "
"latest-candidate writes, cancellation effect tracking, and receipt-"
"matched redacted outputs. Audit events for create, movement, and "
"valuation use the literal actor `runtime`; if human-level attribution is "
"required, this module does not carry that identity into those event "
"calls. The direct `InventoryService` also has `show` and `remove`, but "
"the registered operation set in this chunk has no corresponding "
"registered show/remove worker; synthesis should trace whether another "
"authorized entrypoint exposes them. Event writes after ledger writes are "
"not atomic, while the worker correctly keeps the effect unknown if an "
"exception interrupts this span. No tests or runtime evidence were "
"inspected here."
msgstr ""

